- crates/archcheck: SPACE's crates/tools/archcheck. Renamed to
  compute-archcheck, given standalone dependency versions, taught to expand
  `<dir>/*` workspace members, and its README and repository test pointed at
  this workspace.
- smoke/compute_smoke: SPACE's space_smoke framework (__init__, __main__,
  model, registry, runtime, suite, sharding, fixtures and
  invariants/lifecycle) and its E2B-compatible scenarios
  (scenarios/ecw_*). Renamed to compute_smoke; telemetry, Kubernetes
  discovery and control-plane identity checks removed; fixtures, the
  lifecycle invariant and the shard timings rewritten for this host agent's
  API; scenarios kept as they were except where a scenario's header says
  how it was adapted. The adapter (client, services, config), the compute_*
  scenarios and the guest service are new.

Parts of the design of compute-host follow ideas from SPACE (Sandboxed
Platform for Agentic Code Execution), https://github.com/perplexityai/SPACE,
Copyright 2026 Perplexity AI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

- VMs outlive the host agent and are taken back from durable per-VM records
  when it starts again.
- Every guest gets the same fixed address behind NAT in its own network
  namespace, so a guest restored from a snapshot needs no reconfiguration.

No SPACE source code is included in compute-host. Where a file's design
follows SPACE, its header says so.
